Use the training split's top-N glosses for every split.

verify.py selected the N most frequent glosses separately in train, val and
test, and WLASLDataset numbers labels by each split's own sorted vocabulary.
On ASL Citizen (N=1500) the per-split vocabularies share only 532 (val) and
751 (test) glosses with train, so 1.0% of val and 1.2% of test labels mean the
same gloss to the trained model. The paper's split sizes (23365/5282/17798)
are reachable only by applying train's top-N to all splits; per-split
selection gives 23365/6406/19126. Resolved by the assignee on 2026-10-01.

